<title>RUSSIA: Norilsk preferred falls to $12.40.</title>
<headline>Norilsk preferred falls to $12.40.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preferred shares in Russian metals producer Norilsk Nickel sank to $12.40 at 1400 GMT from $13.40 at 1341 GMT, and $13.50 at Friday's close.</p>
<p>Interfax news agency reported earlier that Prime Minister Viktor Chernomyrdin ordered a tender for 38 percent of the company be suspended. The report had not been officially confirmed. The results of the auction were to have been announced on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Norilsk ordinary shares last traded at $15.05 at 1336 GMT.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
